--
N5008 [temp.inst]/3: the implicit instantiation of a class template
specialization instantiates the DECLARATIONS, not the definitions, of its
member classes; [temp.inst]/4: a member function (template)
specialization's definition is instantiated only when it is used, and
[over.match.viable]/3 + [temp.deduct.general]/8: pair's constrained
default constructor template is not viable for pair<symbolish> (no
default constructor), so it is never used.  The front end, instantiating
vector<pair<symbolish>>, also completes the nested member class `storage'
whose data member has type pair<symbolish>, and in doing so instantiates
pair's default constructor template's body, fails on `first()' ("found no
match for symbol 'symbolish'") and reports it dropped.  Removing the
nested class (or giving vector a plain member of the element type) made
the drop disappear.  Cause: __is_constructible(T) (is_default_constructible)
was always true for a class type, so the constrained constructor was not
removed ([temp.deduct.general]/8) and its body was instantiated; fixed with
cpp11_is_constructible_class_without_default_constructor.  libstdc++: vector::_Temporary_value::_Storage and
pair's `template <class _U1 = _T1, ..., enable_if<__and_<
__is_implicitly_default_constructible<_U1>, ...>>> pair()'
(stl_pair.h:543, 8 cbmc-cpp descs in the round-163 audit);
test_libstdcxx.desc is the libstdc++ program.  Header-free (from the cvise
reduction in /tmp/r163/red/kb_D1).  Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot
bin51).
